	STRING ASIS	BLANKS OFF*******************************************************************                     The Print Manager *                 Epson Driver  v2.0** May 1988*    This driver is originally developed by StyleWare, Inc. using the ImageWriter *    Driver v2.0 as its basis.** v 1.0* June 15, 1988           Suki Lee*    Converted StyleWare's source from APW to MAX. ** June 30, 1988	      Suki Lee*    Made changes to this driver to reflect bug fixes and other modifications done*    to the ImageWriter driver since 2.0 release.*    These changes include:*       - ReOrganized code so opening of the port is done only once at LLDStartUp *         time.*       - Added the filtering of C cedilla in LLDText.** July 25, 1988           Suki Lee  *    Bug fix:*       - The printer name string is "imagewriter". If AppleTalk is chosen, Image-*         Writers on the network can be selected. Changed the string to "epson" so*         no printers can be found, since Epson are not AppleTalk compatible.*       - When printing in Better Text mode, some color text were not printed. Fixed*         the logic in MakePattern, which calculates the dot pattern for color mapping,*         so the correct branch is taken for 640 mode high resolution. Also changed*         the names of some of the branch labels for clarity.** August 5, 1988          Suki Lee*    Bug fix:*       - The "darker" checkbox in job dialog causes problem with some colors not*         being printed. It was originally the color option in the ImageWriter driver.*         Since Epsons have no color capability and "darker" doesn't really improve *         print quality, it is removed from the dialog. Also commented out code in *         StartLLD which checks the corresponding bit in the print record.*       - Use GetCursorAd before the WaitCursor call and use SetCursor instead of *         InitCursor when done to restore the original cursor.** -----------------------------------------------------------* Version 2.0** d1* November 28, 1988        Suki Lee**    Two new calls are added: PrGetPrinterSpecs, which returns the printer's type and*    its characteristics (only color capability is defined for now) and PrGetPgOrientation*    which returns either portrait or landscape. These calls are needed by IIGS HyperCard*    printing.** d2* December 15, 1988    Suki Lee*    Added new header to denote this as a driver which support the new calls PrGet-*    PrinterSpecs and PrGetPgOrientation (and any subsequent new calls). This header*    is 2 words long: first word is 0 followed by a call count word.*     *    Fixed the jump to an incorrect exit routine in PrPixelmap if unsafe to proceed.*    The correct routine is Exit10, not Exit8.* * d3* January 19, 1989     Suki Lee*    Added a new input parameter, handle to the print record, to PrGetPgOrientation.* January 24, 1989     Suki Lee*    Modified PrGetPgOrientation to use Exit4 instead of Exit0 since a long parameter*    has been added.** d4* February 6, 1989     Suki Lee*    Modified PrValidate so that it will no longer call CiXMetrics if the print record*    is valid for the printer type and is the correct version. This was not necessary *    and caused problems for applications that want to modify fields in the record such*    as the page rectangle. * February 8, 1989     Suki Lee*    Added in code in PrPicFile to check the size of Quick Draw's buffer if Better Text*    is requested. If the buffer is too small, we grow the buffer to what we need and *    restore it back to the original size.* February 10, 1989    Suki Lee*    Bug fix in PrValidate: the print record handle is now dereferenced before using.* * d5 * February 23, 1989    Suki Lee*    Further bug fix in PrValidate: PtrToHand call is changed to BlockMove since the *    print record handle has been deferenced. An error was being returned from the*    PtrToHand call, causing the code to display the dialogs to be skipped.* * d6* March 8, 1989        Suki Lee*    Added code in PrValidate to copy the print record into the local data stroage area *    since the driver code works off the local copy of the print record.** March 9, 1989        Suki Lee*    Modified PrPicFile to use rPage data from PrInfo subrecord instead of PrInfoPt. *    The application may modify rPage between pages and since PrInfoPt is designated *    as reserved in the reference manual, the data there may not be accurate.**    Added constant values for iHRes and iVRes in landscape mode. Added code to modify*    these values based on page orientation in CiXmetrics.** March 14, 1989       Suki Lee*    Added initialization of two variables: ZeroPage and SCBValue in PrValidate. This is *    a measure to safeguard against cases where the application enters the print loop *    without calling PrDefault, PrStlDialog or PrJobDialog, where these variables are *    currently being initialized.*    * March 15, 1989       Suki Lee*    Modified the horizontal print head movement code in MovePen to take in account the *    case where the counter for the loop to send spaces starts out at 0. This bug caused*    draft mode to spit out blank pages when some documents are printed.*** d7* March 21, 1989       Suki Lee*    Modified MovePen code to adjust the movement of the print head. Epson printers do*    not have paper reverse capabilities, so the code to reverse the paper is removed*    and printing will occur on the current line. Also, the LX model does not support*    absolute position of the print head, so movement to the right is simulated with *    spaces. The old code calculated the number of spaces based on the left margin*    instead of at the end of the last printed string thus causing large gaps to appear.*    Any movement to the left is ignored and will print from current horizontal position.** March 29, 1989       Suki Lee*    Modified band buffer allocation code to find MaxBlock and if it is larger than 64K,*    we use 64K, else we use the maxblock size. This created a minor problem where an *    entire 8 1/2 x 11 page can fit inside of one band and the idleproc which checks for*    cancel is called each band in the high level routines. A new routine LLDIdleProc is *    implemented so the idleproc can be called from the low level routines, taking care *    of D page swapping and proper stack clean up. This new routine also allows for *    cancelling of printing if there is a printer error.** d8* April 25, 1989       Suki Lee*    Modified InsertPaperAlert to display arrow cursor instead of restoring the cursor*    set by the application, since some applications set the watch cursor before entering*    the print loop.** d9* May 2, 1989          Suki Lee*    Revert PrValidate to recalculating the whole print record each time, so applications can *    modifiy one field and have the rest of the record be consistent. Change code in PrOpenDoc*    to just look at the type and version field of the print record instead of calling *    PrValidate. This is needed for Iduna printing.** d10* May 15, 1989         Suki Lee*    Idleproc pointer in the print record is not set up correctly with the default idleproc*    in draft mode. Added set up code in PrOpenDoc and PrPixelMap. Similar to BRC #48527.*    Also added error checking code so that PrPixelMap printing can use the LLDIdleProc to*    cancel out print job. Similar to BRC #48936** d11* May 19, 1989         Suki Lee*    Landscape prints garbage if the buffer size is larger than the standard size. Added code *    to use only standard buffer if landscape is selected. BRC #48937** May 25, 1989         Suki Lee*    Fixed a cut and paste error in PrPicfile where the wrong offset to the print record is used.** June 2, 1989	   Suki Lee*    Added code to pass the newly added ClosePicture error to the application.** June 5, 1989	   Suki Lee*    Added initialization of variable ZeroPage and SCBValue in PrOpenDoc as well, since some apps *    do not call anything else before the print loop. *************************************************************************************************************************************                    Copyright 1986-1989*                    Apple Computer, Inc.*                    All Rights Reserved******************************************************************	Print off	INCLUDE 'all.macros'	INCLUDE 'epson.macros'	INCLUDE 'e16.Dialog'	Print on;------------------------------------------;; Equates from procedure ;;------------------------------------------VersionNb	equ $0200	; Version 2.0;; error codes;PortNotOn	equ $1302NoPrintRecord	equ $1303;------------------------------------------------------------------------------;; Global and Zero Page Equates;;------------------------------------------------------------------------------True	equ $FFFFFalse	equ $0000BTBuffSize	EQU 320	; the size we need the Quick Draw buffer to be		; for Better Text is twice the scan line width	mem64k	equ $FFFF	; 64 k bytes of memoryTemp1	equ 0	Temp values to dereference easilyTemp2	equ temp1+4	4hPicList	equ temp2+4	apPicList	equ hPicList+4	eOurport	equ pPicList+4	12hOurport	equ OurPort+2	14hNewPic	equ hOurport+4	18ourStatus	equ hNewPic+4	1chStatus	equ ourStatus+2	1ehport	equ hStatus+4	22UserId	equ hPort+4	26hscreenport	equ userId+2	28pscreenport	equ hscreenport+4	2chprbuf	equ pscreenport+4	30pprbuf	equ hprbuf+4	34PZ_PrStatus	equ $C0PZ_pPrPort	equ PZ_PrStatus+4PZ_hPrint	equ PZ_pPrPort+4TPrintsize	equ 140StatRecSize	equ 28* Error CodesnoErr	equ 0iIOAbort	equ -27iMemFullErr	equ -108iPrAbort	equ 128;------------------------------------------;; Equates from procedure table;;------------------------------------------HandleReal	equ $F4PointerReal	equ $F8;--------------------------------------------------------